window.docContents[116].resolve({"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Ultra/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Ultra-1-0":{"contents":"Limits along an ultrafilter\n\nFor a sequence (x_k) in the unit ball of X and a free ultrafilter \\mathcal U on \\mathbb N, z(f)=\\lim_{k\\to\\mathcal U}f(x_k) defines a point z of the unit ball of X^{**} (eq:z), and the canonical extension at z is an iterated limit along \\mathcal U (eq:ulpartial). Lower bounds that hold at every strictly increasing tuple of indices survive these limits.\n\n\n","context":"","header":"LindenstraussPolynomials.Ultra","id":"/LindenstraussPolynomials/Ultra/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___Ultra-1-0"}});